    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-73508",
      "knowledge_point_id": "552973a7-4ab5-5918-83f4-15ee0e3ee052",
      "knowledge_point": "Differentiating an Inverse Sine Function",
      "problem": "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)=8\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡({e}^{x}).$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of arcsine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[8\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡({e}^{x})] \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{({e}^{x})}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1-{e}^{2x}}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{1-{e}^{2x}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
