      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of arcsine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5+9\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x) \\\\  & =0+9\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x) \\\\  & =0+9\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
