      "knowledge_point_id": "552973a7-4ab5-5918-83f4-15ee0e3ee052",
      "knowledge_point": "Differentiating an Inverse Sine Function",
      "problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$  for $f(x)=4\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x).$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of arcsine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x)) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
