    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-73488",
      "knowledge_point_id": "93a44f44-0998-5857-9b12-de8998e370fd",
      "knowledge_point": "Differentiating an Inverse Cosine Function",
      "problem": "Calculate ${f}^{′}(x)$  for $f(x)=5-2\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of arccosine is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5-2\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x) \\\\  & =0-2\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x) \\\\  & =-2(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
