    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-19071",
      "knowledge_point_id": "c5582e8b-3870-5a32-b15e-62b8f8306ce6",
      "knowledge_point": "Differentiating Inverse Trigonometric Functions Using the Product or Quotient Rule",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the quotient rule, using the formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ and applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3}))-\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-({x}^{3})^{2}}})\\cdot (3{x}^{2})-\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{x})}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{6}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arccos}⁡({x}^{3})}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
