      "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the quotient rule and using the formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$  we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}) & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})}{{({e}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x\\cdot {e}^{x}}{{e}^{2x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x)}{{e}^{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x}{{e}^{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
