      "knowledge_point_id": "c5582e8b-3870-5a32-b15e-62b8f8306ce6",
      "knowledge_point": "Differentiating Inverse Trigonometric Functions Using the Product or Quotient Rule",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3})}{{x}^{2}+5}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+5)(1+4{x}^{6})}\\,-$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3})$",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the quotient rule, using the formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ and applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3})}{{x}^{2}+5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(({x}^{2}+5)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3}))-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3})\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+5))}{({x}^{2}+5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(({x}^{2}+5)\\cdot \\frac{1}{1+(2{x}^{3})^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3})\\cdot 2x)}{({x}^{2}+5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{({x}^{2}+5)(6{x}^{2})}{1+4{x}^{6}}-2x\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3}))}{({x}^{2}+5)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+5)(1+4{x}^{6})}-\\frac{2x}{({x}^{2}+5)^{2}}\\,\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2{x}^{3}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
