      "problem": "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ if  $f(x)=\\frac{{arctan}^{2}⁡(5x)}{{x}^{2}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Applying the quotient rule, using the formula for the derivative of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x$ and applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\frac{{arctan}^{2}⁡(5x)}{{x}^{2}}] \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x))-(2x){arctan}^{2}⁡(5x)}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)\\cdot \\frac{5}{1+(5x)^{2}}-(2x){arctan}^{2}⁡(5x)}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5x)}{{x}^{2}(25{x}^{2}+1)}-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}}\\cdot {arctan}^{2}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
